    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "What types of flanges does Remax Forge supply to Solan?",
        "a": "Remax Forge supplies the complete range of ASME B16.5 and B16.47 flanges to Solan: Weld Neck (WNRF), Slip-On (SORF), Blind (BLRF), Socket Weld, Threaded, Lap Joint, Long Weld Neck, and Spectacle Blind flanges. For Solan's Pharmaceutical Manufacturing sector, we particularly recommend SS 316L/304L (pharma-grade) and Carbon Steel A105 material grades in Class 300 to 2500 ratings. All flanges comply with ASME B16.5 for sizes \u00bd\" to 24\" and B16.47 for 26\"\u201360\" large-bore applications."
      },
      {
        "q": "Which material grades are most suitable for Solan's Pharmaceutical Manufacturing industry?",
        "a": "For Solan's Pharmaceutical Manufacturing applications, we recommend: SS 316L/304L (pharma-grade), Carbon Steel A105. For high-temperature services (above 400\u00b0C) in Solan's Pharmaceutical Manufacturing plants, Alloy Steel F11/F22/F91 grades are standard. For corrosive environments, SS 316L or Duplex 2205 is recommended. Our team provides free material selection consultancy for Solan-based project requirements \u2014 contact us with your P&ID specifications."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does Remax Forge supply IBR-approved flanges and fittings to Solan?",
        "a": "Yes. Remax Forge & Fittings manufactures IBR (Indian Boiler Regulations) approved flanges and buttweld fittings for Solan's boiler and pressure vessel applications. IBR compliance is mandatory for steam boilers operating above 3.5 kgf/cm\u00b2 in India. Our IBR-approved products include Weld Neck Flanges in A105, F11, F22, F91 grades, and Buttweld Elbows/Tees for steam lines. We supply IBR form II certificates with all applicable products dispatched to Solan."
      },
      {
        "q": "What is the typical delivery timeline for orders dispatched to Solan?",
        "a": "Road via NH-5; 3-4 day delivery. For ex-stock items (standard sizes in A105, SS 304/316 grades), dispatch from Mumbai warehouse happens within 24-48 hours of order confirmation. Custom or special alloy orders typically require 7-15 working days for manufacturing. We coordinate with specialized freight partners for reliable delivery to Solan and provide real-time shipment tracking. Contact our sales team at +91 97699 83108 for Solan-specific lead time confirmation."
      },
      {
        "q": "What quality documentation do you provide with shipments to Solan?",
        "a": "Every shipment to Solan includes: (1) Mill Test Certificate (MTC) as per EN 10204 3.1 from NABL-accredited labs, (2) Dimensional Inspection Reports as per ASME B16.5/B16.47/B16.11, (3) Hydrostatic Test Certificates, (4) PMI (Positive Material Identification) reports by XRF analysis, (5) Heat Number traceability on all components, (6) Packing list with item-wise heat number mapping, (7) IBR Form II certificate (for applicable products). This complete traceability package is essential for EPC contractors and PSUs procuring for Solan's regulated industries."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can Remax Forge customize flange dimensions or special alloys for Solan projects?",
        "a": "Yes. Remax Forge's CNC precision machining facility handles custom forging requirements for Solan's unique project specifications. We can manufacture: non-standard bore dimensions, special face finishes (RTJ ring grooves, Tongue & Groove, Male-Female), large-bore flanges beyond ASME B16.47 (up to 72\"), special alloys including Inconel 625, Hastelloy C-276, Monel 400, Super Duplex 32750/32760, and Alloy 20. Send us your drawing or specification and we will provide a quotation within 48 hours."
      }
    ],
